  "description": "Stage W2c (ARCHITECTURE decision 40): a service follows a running curve from call to call, x10 (one second a tick). Track a(0,1)-b(1,1)-c(2,1)-d(3,1)-e(4,1)-f(5,1)-g(6,1); Alpha(1,0) has platform b, Beta(3,0) d, Gamma(5,0) f; 1024 world units a link. setTrainPerformance checks the train, then that it runs no service, then the performance (a coast that does not slow less than the braking, or a top speed of 0, is invalidTrainPerformance); setLinePerformance checks the line, then the performance. A line plans each leg in the least whole second its performance builds a curve for: Express (Alpha, Gamma, 4 links, 4096) with the standard performance (1.5 and 2.5 km/h a second, 1/a + 1/b = 0.06 s\u00b2 a unit) takes sqrt(2 x 4096 x 0.06) = 22.2 s, so 23, never reaching 110 km/h; with express (1.8 and 2.9 km/h a second, 0.050647) 20.4, so 21; with 2 minutes at each end 286 and 282 s, 5 minutes either way. Local has the metro game's performance (3.96 and 4.68 km/h a second: 70.4 and 83.2 units a second\u00b2, 80 km/h) and runs Alpha 0/1, Beta 2/2, Gamma 2/4 turning round, Alpha 10/10 (minutes). Started at 0, it dwells at Alpha (doors open by 8, closing from 51) and leaves at 60. Run 1 takes the 60 s its timetable gives it, from the scheduled departure to the scheduled arrival: {start 60, length 2048, seconds 60}, at Beta at 120, on time. Beta is between the ends: least dwell 36 s, it leaves at 156, 36 s late. Run 2 is given 0 s, which no curve fits, so it takes the least, sqrt(2 x 2048 x 0.026224) = 10.4, so 11 s: {156, 2048, 11}; it accelerates for about 4 s, so 1 and 3 s after leaving it has come a x t\u00b2 / 2 = 35.2 and 316.8 units, 35 and 316; it reaches Gamma at 167, 47 s late, lateness 37 a second after leaving (late since 120). Held at Gamma with a rate of 0, it still leaves at 240 (doors closing from 231), turned round to face west, and as it cannot follow its run {240, 4096, 360} (10 units along after a second) it drops it at once: a travelling service with no run. Given its rate back at 600, it sets off from a stand over the way left, 4096, as fast as it can: sqrt(2 x 4096 x 0.026224) = 14.7, so 15 s, {600, 4096, 15}; 35 and 316 units after 1 and 3 s again; at Alpha at 615, 15 s late, where its service ends at 657 (least dwell 42 s at the last stop: closing from 648).",
